---
description: Saving media made with Masonry into this project
alwaysApply: false
---

When a Masonry tool returns an image, video or audio file that is meant for
this project, save it under the folder the project already uses for media
(for example `public/`, `assets/` or `static/`), with a lowercase, hyphenated
name that says what it shows. Reference it from code by that path, and keep
the Masonry link in a comment only when the person asks for provenance. Don't
commit large videos when the project ignores media in git.
